3.2 Official releases. Section 3(c) covers using Oeca yourself, whether for
personal matters, work or study. It does not cover installing, deploying or
providing Oeca for other people, for example across the computers of a school
or business; that requires the Licensor's permission.

Making the source code publicly available does not grant any rights beyond
those stated in this section, those that GitHub's Terms of Service require,
and those that applicable law provides (section 6).


